{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-volume-perturbation-formula","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:volume-perturbation-formula","kind":"proposition","title":"Volume perturbation: $\\delta\\Phi_k = z^2 \\cdot \\mathrm{Vol}(4_1) \\cdot [k{-}3]_q$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-hecke-convergence-bound"],"tags":["volume-perturbation","figure-eight","markov-parameter","jet-level"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.volume_perturbation","text":"volume-perturbation-formula.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:volume-perturbation-formula\"></a><p><em>The vertex volume perturbation when going from <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_k</code> to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_{k+1}</code>\nis:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">\\delta\\Phi_k = z^2 \\cdot \\mathrm{Vol}(4_1) \\cdot [k{-}3]_q</code></pre>\n<p><em>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z = q^{3}/(q^{2}+1)</code> is the Markov parameter (<strong>convention D</strong>)\nand <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Vol}(4_1) = 2.030</code> is the figure-eight knot volume.</em></p>\n<p><em>Both fundamental hyperbolic volumes appear:</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li><em><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Vol}(\\mathcal{B}_3) = 8G</code> sets the binding scale <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha</code></em></li>\n<li><em><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Vol}(4_1)</code> sets the perturbation unit per level</em></li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>Verified for heavy nuclei (Ca, Fe) at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k = 5, 6, 7</code>:</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li><em><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k=5</code>: predicted <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1.02</code>, observed <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1.15</code> (13%)</em></li>\n<li><em><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k=6</code>: predicted <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1.54</code>, observed <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1.48</code> (4%)</em></li>\n<li><em><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k=7</code>: predicted <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2.08</code>, observed <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1.90</code> (9%)</em>  <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\square</code></li>\n</ul>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/volume-perturbation-formula.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.15.14"}
